*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Molecule: H6 chain, R = 1.0 Angstrom
* Basis: ANO-RCC-MB
* Symmetry: C1
* Features tested: the CI-space record of JobIph/HDF5 (CI_SPACE) with a
*                  GAS reference: SA-GASSCF (3 spaces of 2 orbitals, 2 roots),
*                  then MC-PDFT from the JobIph and from the HDF5 file; the
*                  same space as RAS (RAS1 2 orbitals with 2 holes, RAS2 2,
*                  RAS3 2 with 2 electrons), started from the GAS orbitals,
*                  and MC-PDFT: the same energies to about 1e-6 (the GAS run
*                  stops at the default convergence thresholds)
* Responsible person: Roland Lindh
* Comments: MC-PDFT describes a GAS reference by the active orbitals of the
*           record; CASPT2, RASSI and MCLR stop on a GAS reference.
*--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
>> RM -FORCE TEST_HDF5
>> IF ( $MOLCAS_DRIVER = UNKNOWN_VARIABLE )
>>   EXPORT MOLCAS_DRIVER=molcas
>> ENDIF
>> SHELL $MOLCAS_DRIVER have_feature hdf5 || touch TEST_HDF5
>> IF ( -FILE TEST_HDF5 )
>>   EXIT 36
>> ENDIF

&GATEWAY
 coord
6

H 0.0 0.0 0.0
H 0.0 0.0 1.0
H 0.0 0.0 2.0
H 0.0 0.0 3.0
H 0.0 0.0 4.0
H 0.0 0.0 5.0
 basis=ANO-RCC-MB
 Group=NoSym
&SEWARD

&RASSCF
 nActEl = 6
 Inactive = 0
 GASSCF
 3
 2
 2 4
 2
 4 6
 2
 6 6
 Spin = 1
 CIRoot = 2 2 1

&MCPDFT
 FUNC = T:PBE

&MCPDFT
 FileOrb = $Project.rasscf.h5
 FUNC = T:PBE

&RASSCF
 Inactive = 0
 RAS1 = 2
 RAS2 = 2
 RAS3 = 2
 nActEl = 6 2 2
 Spin = 1
 CIRoot = 2 2 1

&MCPDFT
 FUNC = T:PBE
>>FILE checkfile
